Avoid doing useless things. :) This means you don't need..

1) ..300 HP.
2) ..-40 AC.
3) ..to kill every monster, or even close to it. (this is especially
true on the run up)
4) ..to explore every single level of the game.
5) ..to explore dungeon levels N to Castle-1, where N is some number
around 10. (usually dependent upon Sokoban)
6) ..to traverse Gehennom more than once. (as was expounded
elsethread)
7) ..to get +7 Grayswandir and a +7 silver saber.
8) ..max luck.
9) ..to slowly traverse many special levels. (Sanctum in and out
trick, jump across Astral, dig down past Medusa, etc)
10) ..a whole lot to get to the wand of wishing.

It *really* helps to have..

1) ..practice.
2) ..teleport control and intrinsic teleportitis.
3) ..conflict.
4) ..jumping.
5) ..spells.
6) ..a decent number of levelports.
7) ..a good handle on the travel commands. (this is the only tip aimed
specifically at realtime and not turns!)
8) ..a good handle on how to do the Planes painlessly. (so you're not
tempted to overprepare)
9) ..Elbereth.
10) ..a good bones pile. (err..)
10) ..wraith corpses. (especially to get to XL 14.. early castle means
early quest)

Feel free to ask more pointed questions! I'm always happy to share the
little nuggets I've gleaned.

